      h2 New look and feel @345,17,154,21
      text All colors have been carefully and manually redefined for a more contrasted, neutral (less bluish) look and feel. @345,50,154,122
      text The default color theme is much more accessible. Most colors now follow the WCAG 2.1 AAA standard, and some secondary muted colors follow the WCAG 2.1 AA standard. @345,184,154,203
      text Focus states have been improved for more consistency and contrast, and spacings have been reduced for a sleeker and more neutral style. @345,399,154,142
      h2 Easier customization# @345,553,154,43
      text We have refactored all files to make it easier for you to compile your version of Pico with . All modules can now be enabled or disabled using . @345,608,154,142
      text .scss @345,762,154,20
      link SASS /docs/sass @345,794,154,20
      link @use https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/use @345,826,154,21
      text We added more , now totaling over 130, to easily create a unique look and feel, enhancing design flexibility. @345,859,154,121
      link "CSS variables" /docs/css-variables @345,992,154,21
      h2 Color palette# @345,1025,154,21
      text Pico v2 comes with to help you personalize your brand design system. The colors can be imported into any file, and a new stylesheet with all the color utilities is provided. @345,1058,154,183
      link "380 manually crafted colors" /docs/colors @345,1253,154,40
      text .scss @345,1305,154,21
      h2 Better breakpoints# @345,1338,154,42
      text We have updated the to follow the width of standard devices and added a new breakpoint for larger screens. @345,1392,154,122
      link breakpoints /docs/container @345,1526,154,20
      h2 Group component# @345,1558,154,43
      text With (), you can now stack forms elements and buttons horizontally. @345,1613,154,81
      row @345,1706,154,20
        link group /docs/group @345,1706,40,20
        text role="group" @397,1706,87,20
      h2 Conditional Styling# @345,1738,154,43
      text is a powerful feature that allows you to apply styles selectively by wrapping elements in containers, which is ideal for mixed-style environments. This method restricts styling to designated sections, making it particularly useful for combining multiple stylesheets or components seamlessly. @345,1793,154,304
      link "Conditional Styling" /docs/conditional @345,2109,154,21
      text .pico @345,2142,154,20
      h2 Version picker# @345,2174,154,21
      text Play with the , which offers 20 precompiled color themes accessible via CDN for all Pico versions. The total number of combinations is over 100. @345,2207,154,162
      link "Version Picker" /docs/version-picker @345,2381,154,21
      h2 Breaking changes# @345,2414,154,42
      h3 CSS Vars @345,2468,154,19
      text All are prefixed with to avoid collisions with other CSS frameworks or your vars. We also added new CSS variables and renamed some to follow a consistent pattern. @345,2499,154,162
      link "CSS custom properties" /docs/css-variables @345,2673,154,21
      text pico- @345,2706,154,20
      text {component}-{state}-{property} @345,2738,154,20
      h3 SCSS files @345,2770,154,19
      text We renamed and moved many .scss files. If you import Pico modules, you need to update your paths. @345,2801,154,102
      h3 Buttons @345,2915,154,18
      text are not by default anymore. Only form buttons are full-width to be consistent with other form elements. @345,2945,154,102
